A||||4||JetroGT||Fuel pump keeps running.
Z||000000||JetroGT||07-14-99||10:43 PM||||Ok. I recently bought another Fiero. It's an 86 SE V6. Everything was working ok. Then I Rebuilt the top half of the engin, manifolds, heads, plenum, valve covers, throttle, ect. Now that I have it all back together the fuel pump will run with the ignition off intermitently. I have already swaped the fuel pump relay and I tried disconecting the oil pressure sensor to see if it was running through that. No luck.<br>For now I have to pull the fuse to stop it.<br>Any suggestions?
Z||000001||lowCG||07-15-99||12:02 AM||||Try disconnecting the relay,if it still does it,trace the wires to the source.(?)<br>Make sure the A/C relay isn't being used as a Fuel pump relay,don't know how this would affect things,but maybe.<br>Good luck
Z||000002||JetroGT||07-15-99||10:46 PM||||The pump has stoped running with the ignition off. If it had kept running I was going to pull the tank and look at the connector on the pump. I'll keep crossing my fingers for now!
Z||000003||Cooter||07-16-99||01:07 PM||||Jetro- You still need to invistigate this problem. Things that fix themselves have a nasty habit of tearing up by themselves also.
Z||000004||terryk||08-04-99||10:39 AM||||Probably the sender at the engine. The FP backup switch is stuck closed. Mine did this. ~$35. You will need to remove the battery to be able to get a wrench on the block and sender to remove it.
